WEBVTT

1
00:00:27.833 --> 00:00:30.633
- It's freezing!
- We're getting soaked!

2
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.800
- Let's duck in there!
- Ah! Dedenne, stay still!

3
00:00:46.766 --> 00:00:49.500
- Whoa!
- Man, what a storm.

4
00:00:49.566 --> 00:00:53.666
- It came up so suddenly.
- I hate thunder.

5
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.900
Huh?

6
00:00:57.966 --> 00:01:01.400
Let's ask if we can stay here until it stops raining.

7
00:01:01.466 --> 00:01:04.133
- Guys, the door's open. Yay!
- Huh?

8
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.500
Bonnie, you can't just go in there.

9
00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:12.666
Anybody home? Hello! Can we stay here until it stops raining?

10
00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:15.166
Excuse us!

11
00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:17.533
Is anybody here?

12
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.833
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

13
00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:30.266
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

14
00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:33.166
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

15
00:01:33.233 --> 00:01:36.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

16
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.166
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

17
00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:42.500
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

18
00:01:42.566 --> 00:01:45.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

19
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.600
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

20
00:01:48.666 --> 00:01:50.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

21
00:01:50.933 --> 00:01:53.933
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

22
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.600
As our heroes continue their journey to Cyllage City

23
00:02:15.666 --> 00:02:18.133
and Ash's second Kalos region Gym battle,

24
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.299
they find themselves caught in a heavy thunderstorm.

25
00:02:22.366 --> 00:02:25.266
- Is anybody in here?
- Pika!

26
00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:28.833
- Hello?
- Sorry to bother you!

27
00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.733
It seems totally deserted.

28
00:02:30.799 --> 00:02:34.766
The exterior's in pretty bad shape, so maybe nobody lives here anymore.

29
00:02:34.833 --> 00:02:37.766
Hey, why don't we just stay here for a while?

30
00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:39.833
I guess so.

31
00:02:40.833 --> 00:02:43.533
Maybe, but this place gives me the creeps.

32
00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.233
- Huh!
- Yeah, me too.

33
00:02:45.299 --> 00:02:48.500
But it's better than getting wet.

34
00:02:48.566 --> 00:02:52.433
I think it feels creepy because there's no light.

35
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.233
Hmm. Looks like it's still working.

36
00:02:56.333 --> 00:02:57.700
Ah!

37
00:02:57.766 --> 00:02:59.766
- That's better.
- Sure is.

38
00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:02.500
- Hey, Clemont. Thanks.
- Oh!

39
00:03:02.566 --> 00:03:05.500
But... I didn't turn them on.

40
00:03:05.566 --> 00:03:08.500
- So then...
- Who did?

41
00:03:08.566 --> 00:03:11.000
- That's kind of weird.
- Nenne?

42
00:03:11.066 --> 00:03:14.566
Uh! Uh! Probably it must have been the sensors!

43
00:03:14.633 --> 00:03:17.566
- Sensors?
- Yeah. Motion detectors.

44
00:03:17.633 --> 00:03:19.733
That's why the lights came on automatically.

45
00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:23.899
It may be an old house, but it must be equipped with the latest technology.

46
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.033
I see!

47
00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.833
Yeah, or maybe we're inside a haunted house.

48
00:03:31.899 --> 00:03:34.600
- Ooh!
- Did I say that?

49
00:03:34.666 --> 00:03:37.966
Uh, let's wait outside until the rain passes.

50
00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:40.033
Great idea!

51
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.033
- Huh?
- What happened?

52
00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.766
- Guys, the door is locked!
- Pika!

53
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:49.133
- No way!
- But it was just wide open.

54
00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.033
It must be the motion detectors closing and locking the doors

55
00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.966
after they're open for a short while.

56
00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:57.266
- But why are they still locked?
- Let me see.

57
00:03:57.333 --> 00:04:02.066
Maybe this is a haunted mansion that grabs people and then eats them.

58
00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.833
- Ooh!
- Did I say that?

59
00:04:04.899 --> 00:04:08.566
Wait! You should never trust anything that can't be explained by science.

60
00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:13.066
This is a huge mansion, so there has to be another way to get out of here.

61
00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.666
Yup. You're right. Let's go and find it!

62
00:04:15.733 --> 00:04:17.166
Pikachu!

63
00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:25.966
- It's a downpour!
- And it happens raining down on us!

64
00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.700
Yeah, I hate when that happens.

65
00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:31.866
Huh? Look!

66
00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:35.366
There's a good chance it's not raining inside that house.

67
00:04:35.433 --> 00:04:37.500
But what if somebody's there?

68
00:04:37.566 --> 00:04:39.533
Then, I'll keep them company.

69
00:04:39.599 --> 00:04:42.133
We're company, too.

70
00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.599
Open the door!

71
00:04:50.666 --> 00:04:54.400
- This home's creep factor's on ten.
- And that's a bad thing?

72
00:04:54.466 --> 00:04:58.866
It'll keep away the riffraff and make this the perfect Kalos frontline hideaway.

73
00:04:58.933 --> 00:05:02.400
Wait a sec. I thought we were getting out of the rain.

74
00:05:02.466 --> 00:05:04.500
Hm. Huh?

75
00:05:04.566 --> 00:05:06.633
Oh! It's an automated window!

76
00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.400
In an old house like this?

77
00:05:08.466 --> 00:05:10.633
Meowth's right. Wait up, Jessie!

78
00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:18.200
Judging by the looks of it, this place has been abandoned forever.

79
00:05:18.266 --> 00:05:19.633
Longer!

80
00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:25.133
Hm. There must be a light switch around here.

81
00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.000
Oh. Thanks for the light, Meowth.

82
00:05:29.066 --> 00:05:31.133
- I didn't do that.
- Huh?

83
00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.033
I'd say everything in this old joint is automated.

84
00:05:34.099 --> 00:05:36.633
- This old house?
- Huh?

85
00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.333
I'm starting to get a bad feeling about this place.

86
00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.466
- You and me both, pally.
- Let's make sure we have an out.

87
00:05:42.533 --> 00:05:44.466
Word up.

88
00:05:44.533 --> 00:05:46.466
- This thing's locked!
- Huh?

89
00:05:49.533 --> 00:05:50.933
It's just a painting.

90
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.666
You're right. It's a portrait.

91
00:05:54.733 --> 00:05:57.433
Maybe she owns this place?

92
00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:03.366
Maybe she's not alive, but she's here anyway, if you know what I mean.

93
00:06:03.433 --> 00:06:06.766
- Did I say that?

94
00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:10.400
-Did you hear that? That sound?

95
00:06:10.466 --> 00:06:14.133
- Yeah, loud and clear!
- I am so through with this place.

96
00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.700
Anybody hear that?

97
00:06:22.766 --> 00:06:25.500
It must be an old grandfather clock ticking away somewhere

98
00:06:25.566 --> 00:06:27.133
and nothing more, I'm sure of it.

99
00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.900
Sounds to me like someone's pounding a stake.

100
00:06:29.966 --> 00:06:32.433
- How come?
- To stop a vampire?

101
00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.366
My mouth's got a mind of its own today!

102
00:06:39.166 --> 00:06:41.633
Uh! It's just a portrait painting.

103
00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.866
Next time, tell me before I freak out.

104
00:06:43.933 --> 00:06:46.099
Hey, did that woman's eyes move?

105
00:06:47.633 --> 00:06:49.266
What is that awful noise?

106
00:06:49.333 --> 00:06:53.433
Like I previously stated, this is an old mansion, so it's really draughty.

107
00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.633
The draught sounds like a whistle and the whistle sounds like someone screaming,

108
00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.166
which is actually quite common.

109
00:06:58.233 --> 00:07:01.799
You're wrong. I have no doubt in my mind that was somebody screaming.

110
00:07:01.866 --> 00:07:03.833
- Serena's right.
- Pika!

111
00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.433
This mansion must be haunted by the spirit of the lady in that painting.

112
00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.799
- Oh!
- There I go again!

113
00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:15.200
We need to get out of here fast.

114
00:07:15.266 --> 00:07:17.733
I thought you were going to make this our hideout.

115
00:07:17.799 --> 00:07:19.900
- I lied. Huh?
- Huh?

116
00:07:19.966 --> 00:07:22.666
Huh? Huh? What... What's that?

117
00:07:30.633 --> 00:07:32.566
Whatever that is has shining eyes!

118
00:07:32.633 --> 00:07:34.900
Well, I'm not about to stick around and check out

119
00:07:34.966 --> 00:07:37.066
whatever it is that Sparky just threw at us.

120
00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:39.566
That was no Poké Ball and I'm no Pokémon!

121
00:07:39.633 --> 00:07:41.700
But I am!

122
00:07:41.766 --> 00:07:43.866
- Another scream!
- Huh!

123
00:07:43.933 --> 00:07:46.599
- Let's find a way out. Huh?
- Pika?

124
00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.200
Es! Es! Es!

125
00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.333
Huh?

126
00:07:54.466 --> 00:07:57.466
- Hey!
- Wait! Bonnie!

127
00:07:57.533 --> 00:07:59.799
Stop!

128
00:08:04.633 --> 00:08:06.700
Huh?

129
00:08:08.366 --> 00:08:11.133
- Where's Bonnie?
- I don't see her anywhere.

130
00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.733
- Bonnie. Where'd you go?
- Pika pika?

131
00:08:13.799 --> 00:08:16.766
Hey!

132
00:08:16.833 --> 00:08:19.666
Did someone just call us?

133
00:08:19.733 --> 00:08:23.400
It's probably whatever's haunting this goofy joint.

134
00:08:23.466 --> 00:08:26.599
Now that you mention it, it does look haunted, doesn't it?

135
00:08:26.666 --> 00:08:28.533
Will you keep your crazy to yourself?

136
00:08:28.599 --> 00:08:31.533
- Hey!
- Bonnie!

137
00:08:31.599 --> 00:08:33.866
She has to be around here.

138
00:08:33.933 --> 00:08:36.533
- Pika. Pika.
- Huh?

139
00:08:39.833 --> 00:08:41.333
- What's wrong with you?
- Pika?

140
00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:44.500
- Did you see something?
- I figured it out.

141
00:08:44.566 --> 00:08:47.699
There must be a Psychic or Ghost-type Pokémon in this mansion.

142
00:08:47.766 --> 00:08:49.833
That's got to be why those lights turned on

143
00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:52.000
and the doors closed all by themselves.

144
00:08:52.066 --> 00:08:54.900
So you think a Pokémon did all of that?

145
00:08:54.966 --> 00:08:58.100
Of course. That certainly would explain all this weird stuff.

146
00:08:58.166 --> 00:09:01.433
Yeah and maybe that thing we saw was actually a Pokémon.

147
00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.633
- A Pokémon?!
- Pika! Pika!

148
00:09:03.699 --> 00:09:07.033
I'd guess the doors and windows wouldn't open up, because that Pokémon

149
00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.866
probably doesn't want us to get out of the mansion just yet.

150
00:09:09.933 --> 00:09:12.466
- Yeah, but why?
- I don't know.

151
00:09:15.933 --> 00:09:18.633
- Hello there!
- Denenne!

152
00:09:18.699 --> 00:09:21.833
Hey, what's your name? Who are you?

153
00:09:23.833 --> 00:09:26.000
Espurr?

154
00:09:26.066 --> 00:09:28.533
Who's that Pokémon?

155
00:09:33.066 --> 00:09:35.233
It's Espurr!

156
00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:48.300
Are you a ghost? Please tell me. Do you live here?

157
00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:54.533
Hm? Oh! Hmm.

158
00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.000
-Hm.

159
00:09:59.666 --> 00:10:03.133
Oh? Ah!

160
00:10:04.233 --> 00:10:06.766
- Espurr!
- Huh!

161
00:10:06.833 --> 00:10:09.199
Ah!

162
00:10:09.266 --> 00:10:12.199
- Oh!
- Nenne ! Nenne! Nenne!

163
00:10:12.266 --> 00:10:13.866
-Nenne! Nenne!

164
00:10:13.933 --> 00:10:17.199
- Ne...
- Oh!

165
00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.800
- Huh? Oh!
- Nenne?

166
00:10:20.866 --> 00:10:24.133
Oh! Hey, how did we do that?

167
00:10:24.199 --> 00:10:26.800
Wait a minute. Was that you who kept us from falling?

168
00:10:26.866 --> 00:10:29.966
- Espurr. Purr! Purr! Purr!
- Wow, thanks!

169
00:10:30.033 --> 00:10:32.233
- Nenne!
- Whoa!

170
00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:35.566
Were you the one who turned on all the lights and then locked the door?

171
00:10:37.199 --> 00:10:39.800
- Why'd you do that?
- Purr!

172
00:10:42.733 --> 00:10:44.699
Purr! Purr!

173
00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:49.300
What's in here?

174
00:10:53.866 --> 00:10:56.800
Oh!

175
00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:01.833
Espurr!

176
00:11:03.566 --> 00:11:07.166
-Nenne! Ne!

177
00:11:07.233 --> 00:11:09.833
- Whoa!
- Es! Espurr!

178
00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:14.333
- Es! Es! Espurr!
- Huh? Okay!

179
00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:20.833
You ready? Ride the Ponyta! Ride the Ponyta!

180
00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:23.699
Bonnie! Where are you?

181
00:11:23.766 --> 00:11:25.433
Where did you go?

182
00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:27.699
- Pika?
- Do you hear that noise?

183
00:11:27.766 --> 00:11:30.933
- Do you think that's Bonnie?
- Let's go check it out.

184
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.266
Bonnie?

185
00:11:33.333 --> 00:11:36.166
- Who's there?
- Pika! Pika?

186
00:11:36.233 --> 00:11:38.666
Prepare for trouble. Such a familiar sound.

187
00:11:38.733 --> 00:11:41.166
And make it double, like Pikachu's around.

188
00:11:41.233 --> 00:11:44.066
To protect the world from fear and loathing.

189
00:11:44.133 --> 00:11:46.300
To unite all people in creepy clothing.

190
00:11:46.366 --> 00:11:48.833
To denounce the evils of blood-curdling screams.

191
00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:51.166
To extend our reach until we burst at the seams.

192
00:11:51.233 --> 00:11:53.500
- Oh! Argh!

193
00:11:53.566 --> 00:11:55.233
- Scared Jessie!
- Jittery James!

194
00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:57.833
Team Rocket blasts off in a terror-filled blitz!

195
00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.100
Oy!

196
00:11:59.166 --> 00:12:02.000
I'd rather be fighting because I'm scared out of my wits!

197
00:12:02.066 --> 00:12:03.533
This is the pits!

198
00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:06.833
Hm! Looks like we've been haunted by the Twerps!

199
00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.033
- Huh?
- Don't ever do that again!

200
00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.500
So you guys were behind all this!

201
00:12:11.566 --> 00:12:13.800
- Behind what?
- All that weird stuff.

202
00:12:13.866 --> 00:12:16.766
- You're dressed up like ghosts.
- We didn't do anything.

203
00:12:16.833 --> 00:12:20.266
We borrowed these tablecloths 'cause we were cold and soaked to the skin!

204
00:12:20.333 --> 00:12:23.833
- Okay, what did you do with Bonnie?
- Huh? What's a Bonnie?

205
00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:27.400
Save it. The first order of business is getting out of this nuthouse.

206
00:12:27.466 --> 00:12:28.500
- Oh!

207
00:12:28.566 --> 00:12:31.533
Something just went bump in the night!

208
00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.633
Wonder what it was.

209
00:12:33.699 --> 00:12:36.633
Looks like we've got visitors!

210
00:12:36.699 --> 00:12:39.566
- We're out of here!
- Maybe it was Bonnie.

211
00:12:39.633 --> 00:12:42.133
Then we'd better go and check it out now.

212
00:12:42.199 --> 00:12:45.400
Sorry. It fell over.

213
00:12:45.466 --> 00:12:47.366
Espurr!

214
00:12:48.466 --> 00:12:51.599
- Wow. It was you!
- Purr! Purr! Espurr!

215
00:12:51.666 --> 00:12:53.566
- Nenne! Nenne!
- Espurr?

216
00:12:55.333 --> 00:12:58.199
That's a pretty pendant.

217
00:12:59.533 --> 00:13:01.333
Espurr!

218
00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:04.900
- Huh?
- Espurr! Espurr!

219
00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:08.400
I've seen that painting before.

220
00:13:11.833 --> 00:13:14.133
Espurr! Espurr! Espurr!

221
00:13:17.533 --> 00:13:20.366
- It's the same pendant!
- Nenne.

222
00:13:20.433 --> 00:13:23.599
- But why!
- Espurr.

223
00:13:23.666 --> 00:13:25.599
- I'm sorry...
- Huh?

224
00:13:25.666 --> 00:13:27.599
That voice!

225
00:13:27.666 --> 00:13:29.599
Hey, that's Bonnie!

226
00:13:29.666 --> 00:13:31.966
Hmm? What are you saying?

227
00:13:32.033 --> 00:13:34.333
- Bonnie!
- Huh?

228
00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.400
There you are. Hi!

229
00:13:36.466 --> 00:13:38.233
- You okay?
- Thank goodness.

230
00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:41.966
Look, Bonnie. You should never ever run off like that.

231
00:13:42.033 --> 00:13:44.199
You have no idea how worried we've been.

232
00:13:44.266 --> 00:13:45.699
I'm so sorry.

233
00:13:45.766 --> 00:13:48.433
- I was playing with that Pokémon.
- Huh?

234
00:13:50.533 --> 00:13:52.699
Espurr, the Restraint Pokémon.

235
00:13:52.766 --> 00:13:55.566
Espurr's psychic energy can travel hundreds of feet,

236
00:13:55.633 --> 00:13:57.300
blasting everything around it.

237
00:13:57.366 --> 00:13:59.033
I knew it!

238
00:13:59.099 --> 00:14:01.500
Es! Es! Espurr! Espurr! Espurr!

239
00:14:01.566 --> 00:14:04.900
It's trying to tell me something, but I can't understand it.

240
00:14:04.966 --> 00:14:07.566
- Hm.
- We were too panicked to think.

241
00:14:07.633 --> 00:14:09.500
- Huh?
- But now it all makes sense.

242
00:14:09.566 --> 00:14:12.566
- Team Rocket?
- Let's put that aside.

243
00:14:12.633 --> 00:14:15.800
None of us are going to be able to get out of here unless we figure out

244
00:14:15.866 --> 00:14:17.333
what Espurr wants from us.

245
00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.566
The man makes sense. Translate, please.

246
00:14:19.633 --> 00:14:23.666
Basically, Espurr says it wants to return the pendant to the lady in the painting.

247
00:14:23.733 --> 00:14:26.733
Espurr! Espurr! Espurr!

248
00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.933
It says she took really good care of Espurr.

249
00:14:38.833 --> 00:14:40.833
For you!

250
00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:46.300
Good, eh?

251
00:14:46.366 --> 00:14:48.266
She gave it some food.

252
00:14:48.333 --> 00:14:54.333
- Here.
- Espurr?

253
00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.933
Do you like it?

254
00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.033
She gave it a ball.

255
00:14:59.099 --> 00:15:01.699
- Espurr!
- I used to play with my children

256
00:15:01.766 --> 00:15:03.966
and grandchildren like this, too.

257
00:15:04.033 --> 00:15:07.333
They used to play together all the time.

258
00:15:13.366 --> 00:15:14.533
Purr? Espurr.

259
00:15:14.599 --> 00:15:17.466
I'm sorry. I'm all right.

260
00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:25.133
My dear pendant, it means so very much to me.

261
00:15:25.199 --> 00:15:28.633
It was a gift from my husband.

262
00:15:28.699 --> 00:15:32.166
Purr. Purr?

263
00:15:32.233 --> 00:15:34.400
- Espurr!
- Do you like it?

264
00:15:34.466 --> 00:15:37.599
In that case, you may hold on to it for a little while.

265
00:15:37.666 --> 00:15:40.133
Make sure you don't lose it, all right?

266
00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:42.966
Purr! Purr! Espurr!

267
00:15:45.533 --> 00:15:48.900
Come visit again anytime!

268
00:15:51.966 --> 00:15:55.699
Es! Espurr! Espurr!

269
00:15:56.699 --> 00:15:58.699
Then one day...

270
00:16:04.333 --> 00:16:09.500
It came to return her beautiful pendant, but she was gone.

271
00:16:10.666 --> 00:16:13.500
I see. So it's been waiting for her.

272
00:16:13.566 --> 00:16:17.233
So it could return her pendant... all this time.

273
00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:19.766
Yeah.

274
00:16:19.833 --> 00:16:21.500
She must have really liked you a lot

275
00:16:21.566 --> 00:16:24.500
if she let you wear that pretty pendant of hers like she did.

276
00:16:24.566 --> 00:16:26.733
Espurr! Espurr! Espurr!

277
00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:30.466
But now Espurr wants to find out where the old lady went off to.

278
00:16:30.533 --> 00:16:33.000
I'm afraid there's no way any one of us would know.

279
00:16:33.066 --> 00:16:34.266
Pika! Pika!

280
00:16:34.333 --> 00:16:37.466
- Hey, Ash, we could try to find out.
- Yeah, we could.

281
00:16:37.533 --> 00:16:39.833
- Pika.
- That's a great idea.

282
00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:42.199
I'm afraid we don't have time for such silliness.

283
00:16:42.266 --> 00:16:44.199
We know the quickest way out of here.

284
00:16:44.266 --> 00:16:47.333
And that's to catch Espurr.

285
00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:50.466
- What are you doing?
- Pumpkaboo, let's go!

286
00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:54.599
- Pump! Pumpkaboo!
- Okay, Inkay!

287
00:16:55.766 --> 00:16:57.866
Inkay! Inkay! Ink!

288
00:16:57.933 --> 00:16:59.500
Now! Use Leech Seed!

289
00:17:04.733 --> 00:17:06.533
-Espurr!

290
00:17:06.599 --> 00:17:09.033
Psybeam, Inkay, and make it a good day!

291
00:17:09.099 --> 00:17:11.833
Inkay!

292
00:17:11.899 --> 00:17:14.366
No!

293
00:17:15.766 --> 00:17:17.766
It's using Protect!

294
00:17:17.833 --> 00:17:19.500
Thanks a lot, Espurr!

295
00:17:19.566 --> 00:17:22.500
Espurr!

296
00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:27.200
-What's going on?

297
00:17:30.166 --> 00:17:32.266
Yes! We finally got out of there!

298
00:17:32.333 --> 00:17:35.100
True, but where are we going next?

299
00:17:35.166 --> 00:17:38.166
- Guess!
- We're blasting off again!

300
00:17:39.166 --> 00:17:42.533
- Espurr, that was great!
- You really got us out of a jam.

301
00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:44.633
I can't believe how powerful you are!

302
00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.100
Espurr! Espurr.

303
00:17:53.399 --> 00:17:54.866
Espurr! Espurr!

304
00:17:54.933 --> 00:17:58.066
Just leave finding the lady who lived here to us.

305
00:18:02.266 --> 00:18:05.133
I wonder if that woman lived here all by herself?

306
00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:08.133
- Hm.
- You talking about Grandma Lacy?

307
00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:11.100
- Huh?
- Uh, Grandma Lacy?

308
00:18:11.166 --> 00:18:13.933
That's her in that painting. She's my grandmother.

309
00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.800
Wow, she's your grandmother?!

310
00:18:15.866 --> 00:18:17.666
Does that mean you own this big house?

311
00:18:17.733 --> 00:18:20.033
That's right. I sure do. My name's Elise.

312
00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:22.399
So, who might you be?

313
00:18:22.466 --> 00:18:25.700
I understand. You knew my grandmother then.

314
00:18:25.766 --> 00:18:28.166
I'm sorry we entered your house without permission.

315
00:18:28.233 --> 00:18:30.933
No problem. I'm glad you were able to get out of the rain.

316
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.100
Grandma Lacy always used to play games with me

317
00:18:34.166 --> 00:18:36.166
when I would come here for a visit, too.

318
00:18:36.233 --> 00:18:39.433
- Just like she did with you.
- Purr! Purr! Espurr!

319
00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.000
Where's your Grandma Lacy now?

320
00:18:42.066 --> 00:18:44.533
I'm afraid she passed away.

321
00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:47.433
Purr? Purr...

322
00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.433
- Nenne?
- Huh.

323
00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.500
I'm sorry.

324
00:18:53.766 --> 00:18:55.933
Huh?

325
00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.933
- Oh!
- Espurr! Espurr! Espurr!

326
00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.600
Espurr wanted to return that pendant to your grandma.

327
00:19:02.666 --> 00:19:07.366
Thank you. This was my grandmother's favorite piece of jewelry.

328
00:19:08.399 --> 00:19:10.866
This old house was scheduled to be torn down soon.

329
00:19:10.933 --> 00:19:12.700
It's in pretty bad shape,

330
00:19:12.766 --> 00:19:15.866
so I came back to see what kind of condition it was in.

331
00:19:15.933 --> 00:19:17.266
But you know what?

332
00:19:17.333 --> 00:19:21.433
After this, after meeting all of you, I think I've changed my mind.

333
00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:24.366
I'm going to renovate this place.

334
00:19:24.433 --> 00:19:26.366
- Purr?
- Now, don't worry.

335
00:19:26.433 --> 00:19:30.200
Grandma Lacy's portrait will stay exactly where it is.

336
00:19:30.266 --> 00:19:33.566
And when it's all finished, I'm going to move in.

337
00:19:33.633 --> 00:19:37.733
And you know what? I'd be thrilled if you'd come and play.

338
00:19:41.466 --> 00:19:45.666
I know! Do you want to go to the cemetery where Grandma Lacy is now?

339
00:19:45.733 --> 00:19:49.833
You can tell her all about the pendant and say goodbye.

340
00:19:49.899 --> 00:19:51.899
Espurr!

341
00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.666
I'm sure you'll take good care of Espurr, right?

342
00:20:03.733 --> 00:20:06.866
Of course. I think Espurr and I will be good friends.

343
00:20:06.933 --> 00:20:10.066
- Take care, okay?
- Espurr!

344
00:20:12.966 --> 00:20:15.633
Two hearts, Espurr's and Elise's,

345
00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.866
connected by Grandma Lacy's pendant.

346
00:20:17.933 --> 00:20:20.233
Our heroes have witnessed yet another bond

347
00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:25.000
between people and Pokémon, as their journey continues!

348
00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.733
You know, I think it would be a whole lot better

349
00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:35.800
if you held on to that pendant, instead of me.

350
00:20:35.866 --> 00:20:38.333
I'm sure that's what Grandma Lacy would want anyway.

351
00:20:44.133 --> 00:20:47.066
It looks perfect!

352
00:20:47.133 --> 00:20:48.500
Purr! Purr! Espurr!

353
00:20:48.566 --> 00:20:50.200
What a pretty flower!

354
00:20:50.266 --> 00:20:51.566
Purr! Espurr!
